          "fact": "The answer incorrectly treats CQ as a finesse against CJ.",
          "explanation": "CA and CK have already won completed tricks. CQ therefore beats every remaining club regardless of CJ's location; the supposed losing finesse and associated contingency are impossible.",
          "quotes": [
            "Continue by leading a low club from South toward dummy’s CQ, using it as a finesse against the unseen CJ",
